    "body": "Closes #103.\n\nImplements ADR-009's stylesheet parser in two commits: rule skeleton first, then declarations.\n\n## Commit 1 — `feat(css)`: rule skeleton\n\n- New module files `renderer/css/stylesheet.{hpp,cpp}`\n- `Stylesheet::parse(std::string_view) -> Stylesheet` — never fails, malformed input is skipped\n- Rule boundary detection via depth tracking (`{` / `}`)\n- Delegates selector parsing to `SelectorList::parse` (ADR-008) — no reimplementation\n- Comment stripping (`/* ... */`) happens **before** rule scanning — required so a `}` inside a comment doesn't close the rule early\n- At-rules (`@media`, `@import`, etc.) are skipped wholesale (deferred per ADR-009)\n- Error recovery: malformed selectors, empty selectors, stray `}` at top level, unterminated rules\n- 14 rule-skeleton tests\n\n## Commit 2 — `feat(css)`: declaration parsing\n\n- Extends `Stylesheet::parse` to populate `Rule::declarations`\n- Splits declaration blocks on top-level `;`, respecting parentheses, brackets, and quotes — a `;` inside `url(...)` or a string does not end the declaration\n- Per declaration: split on first `:`, trim both sides, detect and strip trailing `!important` (case-insensitive, whitespace allowed between `!` and the keyword)\n- Malformed declarations skipped silently: missing `:`, empty property, empty value\n- 14 declaration tests covering every row of ADR-009's behavior table plus edge cases\n\n## Data model (from ADR-009)\n\n```cpp\nstruct Declaration { std::string property; std::string value; bool important; };\nstruct Rule        { SelectorList selectors; std::vector<Declaration> declarations; };\nstruct Stylesheet  { std::vector<Rule> rules; static Stylesheet parse(std::string_view); };\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[css][stylesheet]\"` → **28 cases, 76 assertions, all pass**\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests` → **91 cases, 416 assertions, all pass** (was 77/363 before this PR)\n- `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp` — ADR-007 isolation holds\n- `renderer::dom` untouched — this is text-in, structure-out\n\n## Out of scope (per ADR-009)\n\n- At-rules: `@media`, `@import`, `@font-face`, `@supports`\n- Custom properties (`--x`), `var()`, `calc()`, `rgb()`\n- Shorthand expansion (`margin: 0 1em` stays as a raw string; expansion happens at cascade time)\n\n## Next\n\nWith stylesheet parsing merged, the three inputs to the cascade are all ready: DOM (PR #98), selectors (PR #101), rules (this PR). ADR-010 will define the cascade: given a `Stylesheet` and a `dom::Document`, compute per-element `ComputedStyle`.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-19T17:43:57Z",
